[1m[38;5;231mWhat should "track who logged in" actually do with the value?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mJust include it in the existing log[39m
     [38;5;246mAdd it to the console.log and the returned object. No new code beyond the login function — keeps this genuinely [39m
     [38;5;246mbounded.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Send it to the API call
     [38;5;246mInclude userId in the payload the stub would POST to API_ENDPOINT. Changes the request contract the backend sees.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Persist it somewhere
     [38;5;246mWrite logins to localStorage or a tracking endpoint. This adds a tracking/storage subsystem that doesn't exist yet
